</figure>
<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sweep separates representational scaling from computational failure modes.
For <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}\leq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}\leq 8</annotation></semantics></math>, the QBM produces small but positive <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> values in the
sweep (0.032–0.038). The main experiment (<math id="S5.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}=8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=30</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per
class, 50 epochs) achieves <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0.381" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.381</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0.381</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming that training
sample size and epochs are important confounds in the dimensionality sweep. For
<math id="S5.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}&gt;10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}&gt;10</annotation></semantics></math>, the mean-field approximation collapses <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S5.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, bounding the practical range to <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{h}\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{h}\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math> for exact computation.
Grid size scaling shows sharp <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> degradation: from 0.863 (<math id="S5.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\times 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\times 10</annotation></semantics></math>)
to 0.0025 (<math id="S5.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\times 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\times 50</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.8 </span>Continuous Signal Characterization</h3>

<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="S5.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Entanglement entropy <math id="S5.T9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of self-preservation
weight <math id="S5.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Pearson <math id="S5.T9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.934" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.934</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.934</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S5.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=11</annotation></semantics></math> points, <math id="S5.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{per}}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>per</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{per}}=20</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories each).
Strong positive correlation (<math id="S5.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r|&gt;0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r|&gt;0.8</annotation></semantics></math>) indicates UCIP measures the
<em id="S5.T9.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">degree</em> of self-preservation, not only its binary presence.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T9.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T9.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
