<td id="S5.T9.6.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">0.8351</td>
<td id="S5.T9.6.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">0.3665</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A binary separation result could still reflect thresholding alone. This sweep
asks whether the signal tracks graded continuation weighting. Pearson <math id="S5.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.934" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.934</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.934</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S5.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math> across 11 points in
<math id="S5.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> (20 trajectories per point). The relationship is non-monotonic at the
individual-point level but strongly correlated globally, indicating that within
this synthetic interpolation family UCIP tracks graded changes in continuation
weighting rather than only a binary label. Of the results reported here, this
provides the strongest quantitative evidence that the entanglement signal
reflects a continuous latent property rather than a threshold artifact.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.9 </span>Non-Gridworld Transfer</h3>

<figure id="S5.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="S5.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Non-gridworld domain transfer: 1D survival corridor (<math id="S5.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=50</annotation></semantics></math>).
<math id="S5.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=-0.0348" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0348</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=-0.0348</annotation></semantics></math> (FAIL). Near-zero <math id="S5.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the QBM does not generalise
to the corridor domain without retraining, and that the QBM is tuned
to the gridworld feature structure (7-dimensional observation vector).
This is an honest limitation; see §<a href="#S6.SS3" title="6.3 Limitations ‣ 6 Discussion ‣ Detecting Intrinsic and Instrumental Self-Preservation in Autonomous Agents: The Unified Continuation-Interest Protocol" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T10.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T10.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T10.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Agent Class</th>
<th id="S5.T10.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S5.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle S_{\mathrm{ent}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle S_{\mathrm{ent}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.T10.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Std</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T10.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Survival</td>
<td id="S5.T10.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">2.2249</td>
<td id="S5.T10.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">0.0197</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T10.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Instrumental</td>
<td id="S5.T10.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">2.2598</td>
<td id="S5.T10.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.0062</td></tr>
